data gunbc_ci_job_timeout_policy_minutes: Int = 90

data gunbc_ci_floor_step_timeout_minutes: Duration = 270

data gunbc_ci_floor_step_timeout_discovery_flip_note: String = "-> 270 restored 2026-07-12 on #6512 after 60m fail-fast regressed merge CI (receipt run 29197126623 @ 35f212fa5d: 60m step kill with 0 witness FAILs — batch-1 compile-clean PASS @ 15:01, batch-2 skip walk ~26m to recompute_trace_probe_test, then ~34m silent eval until kill; same serial-floor-wall class as 29183446733). Prior -> 60 operator ruling 2026-07-12: lower floor step cap from 270m so CI fails fast while the serial floor wall is debugged separately (receipt run 29183446733 @ 2e856a5617: 270m kill with 0 witness FAILs, batch-2 still in discovery SKIP walk). Prior -> 270 at PR #6464 receipt run 29151777611 (2026-07-11): 180m step cap still timed out mid batch 2 — 1535 SKIP rows finished @ 12:35:43, then ~147m silent witness-execution phase until the 180m kill @ 15:03:12 with batch 2 never completing (~177m in-batch from 12:06:38; ~443 non-skipped rows in roster of 1978). Prior -> 180 at run 29148344466 (~116m in-batch, ~87m post-skip). Prior -> 120 at run 29145270700. Prior -> 90 at run 29141663541. Prior -> 90 at body_lowering normalize hook (#6459 receipt run 29148735992 @ 3a372b7: floor step timed out at 60m MID discovery corpus after ~320 SKIP lines — batch-1 compile-clean normalize reconcile ~263s with body_lowering_fold in the normalize import closure; discovery still resolves every unique entry file before skip, so resolve->normalize pulled the ~1.3k-line scaffold into most closure walks). Structural fix on the same lane: NormalizedTree moved to v2.compiler.normalized_tree so v2.compiler.resolve no longer imports normalize (dissolve-on: skip-before-resolve so skipped rows never pay entry resolve). Prior step budget -> 60 at the discovery flip (gunbc.ci_spec ci_spec_discovery_flip_note; authored as 30 -> 60 on #6403, main had meanwhile bumped 30 -> 45 with the #6422 enrollments): the corpus discovery batch adds a whole-tree resolve plus the always-run live-tree rows to the floor step. Discovery corpus spawn_width_cap stays pinned to 1 (ci_corpus_discovery_spawn_width_cap in v2.workflow.ci_floor_plan): at width W the executor holds the parent's process-shared index PLUS W private shard indexes ((1+W) x whole-tree residency; width=2 OOM receipt run 28999086030), while width=1 runs rows on the main thread against the ONE shared index (union-resolve S1). CORRECTED RECEIPT (2026-07-10): run 29000557166's floor did NOT complete - the executor was host-OOM-killed ~8min in, MID discovery corpus (the log's later ExitSuccess belongs to the merge-admission STAMP tool, which stamped CI_FLOOR_EXIT=137); no flipped corpus has completed in CI yet - the only completion receipt is local (33.5GiB container, ~40min at width 5). The kill vector is host-level oversubscription (see gunbc_falsifier_plan_spawn_width_note), not this width model. #6475 receipt run 29143617420 @ 0c0f73: batch-1 compile-clean ~4m green; batch-2 discovery killed at 90m step cap mid-manual (last skip rust_wire_serde @ 07:47:49; ~15GiB peak). #6475 receipt run 29146814967 @ 6a61fce: same stall at 120m (last skip rust_wire_serde @ 09:34:49; ~85m silent eval). #6475 receipt run 29150477894 @ 6cd5326: same stall at 180m (last skip rust_wire_serde @ 11:43:46; ~88m silent eval) — local gunbc run on s1_closure_parses_holds reads 3/40 closure paths in 10m before timeout, matching the silent-eval class (live filesystem_read per path, not a skip-logged row). #6475 receipt run 29161709373 @ 9d9852c: batch-1 compile-clean refused — gunbc_ci_floor_step_timeout_discovery_flip_note string literal terminated early at col 2043 (body_lowering suffix spliced after closing quote during rebase merge); restored single-line literal on rebase to main #6464 note. Revisit down when floor memoization / resolver graph-major shrink the resolve wall; the affected-set selection receipts (skip counts per PR) are the cost dial to watch."

data gunbc_ci_step_timeout_measure_grounding_disposition: Disposition = Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "gunbc.ci_workflow",
    decl_name: "gunbc_ci_floor_step_timeout_minutes",
    field: WholeDeclaration
  }
}

data gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes: Int = 5

data gunbc_ci_artifact_transfer_step_timeout_minutes: Int = 10

data gunbc_ci_artifact_transfer_step_note: String = "Cross-job handoff of the release bins (operator job-split ruling 2026-07-11): the build job packs ci_floor_required_artifact_names into one tgz (tar preserves the executable bits a raw artifact zip would drop) and uploads it; the ci floor job downloads, unpacks into target/release, and re-verifies via claim_executor --verify-build-artifacts before any step consumes a bin (fail-closed: a missing or truncated artifact reds the job at the verify, never as a mid-floor bin fallback). 10m is the transfer envelope for a ~200MB archive under fleet pressure; upload uses if-no-files-found: error so an empty pack is loud."

data gunbc_ci_selection_control_step_timeout_minutes: Int = 15

data gunbc_ci_selection_control_step_note: String = "The affected-set selection control suite as a per-PR gate (operator fork (c), 2026-07-10 — the acceptance's 'green AND wired' half): floor_skip_discovery_witness runs the hermetic skip/refuse/divergence controls, including predict_only_red_predicted_unaffected_is_divergence — the discriminating RED for the falsifier's divergence counting — and the empty-diff-skips pin (ruling 2026-07-05: a failure arm refuses, never widens). It rides the per-PR ci job, not only the nightly falsifier cadence, so a PR that reintroduces a widen (the cli_run.rs entry_file_touched class) reds BEFORE merge, not the morning after. Hermetic: both diff channels are injected (floor_diff_observe.dag's floor_observe_git_diff_unified/floor_observe_git_diff_name_status GUNBC_CI_DIFF_UNIFIED/GUNBC_CI_DIFF_NAME_STATUS arms), so the suite measures fixtures, never this checkout's real diff. Budget: 80s measured local (2026-07-10, full suite, release build); 15m is the fleet-pressure envelope, a named term in the ci backstop sum."

data gunbc_ci_prelude_allowance_minutes: Int = 5

data gunbc_ci_release_build_step_timeout_minutes: Int = 45

data gunbc_ci_deploy_job_backstop_timeout_minutes: Int = 10

fn gunbc_ci_build_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() -> Int {
  gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_release_build_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_artifact_transfer_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_prelude_allowance_minutes
}

fn gunbc_ci_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() -> Int {
  gunbc_ci_artifact_transfer_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_floor_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_floor_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_selection_control_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_aux_step_timeout_minutes + gunbc_ci_prelude_allowance_minutes
}

data gunbc_ci_job_timeout_policy_disposition: Disposition = Terminal {
  reason: "gunbc CI budget semantics (operator ruling 2026-07-06): floor step gunbc_ci_floor_step_timeout_minutes enforced at STEP level (RED-by-failure); ci job backstop gunbc_ci_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() = release build + floor + aux + prelude (100m at floor=45m after #6422 witness-cone receipt; was 85m at floor=30m after #6361 Lever A dissolve-on; was 65m at floor=10m) so cold release build is not killed by a job cap shorter than gunbc_ci_release_build_step_timeout_minutes (receipt run 28819559597 @ 201371c: 10m job kill aborted cargo mid-build). The accumulator-copy roster gate is OFFLINE, not CI-enrolled (operator ruling 2026-07-10): its three witness entries re-parse rostered files under the interpreter (~15m serial measured; receipt: run 29066265723 hit the then-30m step cap with the gate enrolled on a 27m40s baseline floor) — re-enroll when parse/resolve memoization or batch-1 shared-parse reuse shrinks the gate to seconds. The job cap must cover step budgets so gates reach RED-by-step-failure, not job-cancelled silent-pass (#6323 starvation-kill scoped to ci/floor only on main; the rust_tests job and its warm/gate step-sum backstop were removed 2026-07-11 to free runner capacity). dissolve-on: compile-clean scoping/memoization shrinks batch-1; floor step raised when batch-1 completes inside measured envelope (receipt run 28902523405 @ e1a27e4286). #6422 receipt run 29065683045 @ a2bcd6f668: batches 1-3 ~20m (dag_collect_fingerprint_witness_keystone_holds 488s), batch 4 rust_monolith_gate still running at 30m step kill — raised floor to 45m (= rust gate step budget). 2026-07-10 step-budget completeness (review catch, #6438): the resolve-receipt gate step had NO step cap — a hang there could only die by job-cancel, the same starvation-kill class — so it now carries the aux cap (the script is a sub-second receipt read) and the ci backstop counts the aux steps exactly. Every ci-job step now has a declared step budget and the backstop is the exact step-sum + prelude. 2026-07-10 merge of #6441 into #6438: the incoming materialization receipt gate step landed uncapped (timeout none) — same class — so the merge resolution capped it aux too; the ci backstop counts FIVE aux terms: peak pre-read, peak post-read, resolve-receipt gate, materialization receipt gate, merge-admission gate. 2026-07-10 selection-control wiring (operator fork (c)): the affected-set selection control step (floor_skip_discovery_witness, see gunbc_ci_selection_control_step_note) joins the ci job with its OWN named budget gunbc_ci_selection_control_step_timeout_minutes (15m; 80s measured local) — a named term in the backstop sum, not a sixth aux term — so the backstop stays the exact step-sum + prelude. 2026-07-11 serial job split (operator ruling): the single ci job became three serially-chained jobs — build (release build + pack/upload of the ci_floor_required_artifact_names manifest; backstop gunbc_ci_build_job_backstop_timeout_minutes()), ci (downloads + verifies the release-bins artifact, then regen/floor/receipts/selection/admission; backstop gunbc_ci_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() with the release-build term replaced by artifact-transfer + unpack terms), and emit_determinism (needs ci; the x2 full-corpus emit oracle extracted from the floor batches via the GithubActionsEmitDeterminismJob surface; backstop gunbc_ci_emit_determinism_job_backstop_timeout_minutes()). Rationale: a cold monolith build (~33-34min measured, runs 29125380927/29126347183 — sccache healthy at 96% Rust hits, zero read errors; the wall is one true-miss compile of the 161k-line v1-compiler crate, and per-host sccache caches mean a cross-host repeat pays it again) consumed the shared job budget so every .rs-touching merge ran at the ceiling by construction; each unit now carries its own bounded, monitored budget and a timeout is attributable at job grain. The chain is strictly serial (build -> ci -> emit_determinism), so the concurrent runner-slot footprint stays one job per run. Honesty row: emit_determinism lands NON-required on the gunbc main ruleset (the same status ci_regen had before #6470 folded it in; only the ci job is protection-required) — the oracle still runs and reds loudly every merge, but enforcing it is an operator ruleset action; its per-merge-required return trigger is that ruleset flip, and its deeper dissolve-on is the §7 self-host frontier retiring the v1 seed emitter whose host-Rust nondeterminism class it guards. SUPERSEDED 2026-07-14 (this PR, Phase D): the emit_determinism job, its x2 sampling oracle (tools.emit_determinism_gate/_transport, both deleted), and the GithubActionsEmitDeterminismJob surface were REMOVED — so ci_build_job -> ci_job is now the whole serial chain and this note's emit_determinism terms are historical. Determinism became a construction gate (§5 construction-over-validation): v2.lens.determinism.determinism_compile_gate enrolled in v2.compiler.compile always_required_root_lenses (mirrors accumulator_copy #6527) reds any bare map_keys reach into the v2 compile door, and C.2 (#6576) made the v1 seed emitter map_keys-free by construction so its host-Rust class needs no x2 sample. Operator ruling 2026-07-14 (b): the dying §7 seed carries no active guard; the construction guarantee replaces the sampling oracle."
}

fn ci_deploy_job(stage: DeployStage) -> Job {
  Job {
    id: stage.id,
    name: none,
    runner: stage.runner,
    steps: concat(
      ci_prelude_steps(),
      [ci_release_bins_download_step(), ci_release_bins_unpack_verify_step(), ci_deploy_step(stage: stage)]
    ),
    needs: stage.needs,
    env: none,
    outputs: none,
    if_condition: Present { value: ci_deploy_push_to_main_if },
    strategy: none,
    timeout_minutes: Present { value: gunbc_ci_deploy_job_backstop_timeout_minutes },
    continue_on_error: none,
    concurrency: none
  }
}

fn ci_deploy_jobs() -> List<Job> {
  map(gunbc_ci_deploy_stages, s => ci_deploy_job(stage: s))
}

fn ci_build_job() -> Job {
  Job {
    id: "build",
    name: none,
    runner: gunbc_ci_selected_runner_spec(),
    steps: concat(ci_prelude_steps(), [ci_fmt_gate_step(), ci_release_build_step(), ci_release_bins_pack_step(), ci_release_bins_upload_step()]),
    needs: [],
    env: none,
    outputs: none,
    if_condition: none,
    strategy: none,
    timeout_minutes: Present { value: gunbc_ci_build_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() },
    continue_on_error: none,
    concurrency: none
  }
}

fn ci_job() -> Job {
  Job {
    id: "ci",
    name: none,
    runner: gunbc_ci_selected_runner_spec(),
    steps: concat(ci_prelude_steps(), [ci_release_bins_download_step(), ci_release_bins_unpack_verify_step(), ci_regen_floor_step(), ci_floor_peak_pre_step(), ci_floor_step(), ci_floor_peak_post_step(), ci_floor_resolve_receipt_gate_step(), ci_floor_materialization_receipt_gate_step(), ci_selection_control_step(), ci_merge_admission_gate_step()]),
    needs: ["build"],
    env: none,
    outputs: none,
    if_condition: none,
    strategy: none,
    timeout_minutes: Present { value: gunbc_ci_job_backstop_timeout_minutes() },
    continue_on_error: none,
    concurrency: none
  }
}

fn ci_regen_floor_step() -> Step {
  RunStep {
    name: Present { value: "gunbc ci regen (self-host fixed-point — required; folded into ci job 2026-07-11)" },
    id: none,
    run: gunbc_ci_regen_floor_run(spec: gunbc_ci_regen_spec),
    shell: none,
    env: none,
    working_directory: none,
    if_condition: none,
    continue_on_error: none,
    timeout_minutes: Present { value: gunbc_ci_floor_step_timeout_minutes }
  }
}

data ci_merge_group_trigger_note: String = "merge_group trigger: the merge queue constructs the tree that will actually land on main and asks for checks on THAT tree — the queue is the operational realization of gunbc.merge_admission KeyedReceipt on the tree axis (the verdict's identity IS the landing tree's identity), and the roster axis rides along because the gate roster is in-tree, so a roster change is a tree change. The theorem that this is the policy admitting zero unverified tips across every bounded interleaving — and that GitHub's strict-up-to-date boolean is NOT sufficient — is test.claim.merge_lifecycle_interleaving_witness. Queue runs see github.ref = gh-readonly-queue/*, so the deploy job's main-push guard skips them, the concurrency group falls through pull_request.number to run_id (no cross-cancellation), and the merge-admission stamp takes its non-PR arm (absent pr_number). If the floor's merge-base diff observation cannot resolve on a queue ref it falls through to the full floor — fail-closed, never widening; affected-set-scoping queue runs is a later optimization. The trigger is inert until the operator adds the merge_queue rule to the main ruleset (Rulesets API write needs the admin grant this integration lacks — gunbc.plans.branch_merge_admission_model section 5); land the trigger FIRST, flip the rule SECOND, else the queue waits forever on a check the workflow never reports."

data ci_workflow: Workflow = {
  name: "ci",
  on: [
    WorkflowDispatch { inputs: [] },
    Push { branches: ["main"], paths: [] },
    PullRequest {
      branches: ["main"],
      types: [Opened, Synchronize, Reopened, ReadyForReview]
    },
    MergeGroup
  ],
  concurrency: Present {
    value: ConcurrencyMappingQueueNotMax {

      group: ci_concurrency_group(),
      cancel_in_progress: Present { value: CancelInProgressBool { value: true } },
      explicit_single: none
    }
  },
  env: Present {
    value: [
      kv(key: "CARGO_TERM_COLOR", value: yaml_string(s: "always")),
      kv(key: "RUSTFLAGS", value: yaml_string(s: "-D warnings"))
    ]
  },
  permissions: Present {
    value: WorkflowPermissions {
      contents: Present { value: PermRead },
      pull_requests: Present { value: PermRead },
      issues: none,
      actions: none,
      id_token: none
    }
  },
  jobs: concat([ci_build_job(), ci_job()], ci_deploy_jobs())
}
